# What does NOT get served, even though it lives in the repo.
#
# wrangler.jsonc points the asset directory at "./" — the repo is the site —
# so by default every file here is a public URL. That was fine while the repo
# was only the site, and stopped being fine once it also held development
# pages, test harnesses and the database schema.
#
# gitignore syntax, read by Cloudflare at deploy time.

# ---- development pages ----
# Neither is linked from anywhere, but an unlinked page is still a URL, and
# demo-plans.html writes straight to the draft key: a visitor who found it
# and pressed the button would lose the guide they were writing. It exists to
# put real plans in front of the editor locally, which does not need the
# public internet.
demo-plans.html
face-offsets.html

# ---- the test harnesses and build scripts ----
# Harmless to read and pointless to serve. serve.ps1 and serve.js are local
# development servers; nobody should be fetching those from the live site.
tools/

# ---- the database ----
# schema.sql is not a secret — it contains no keys, and the policies in it
# are enforced by Postgres whether or not anyone has read them — but there is
# no reason to hand out the table layout and the exact policy predicates.
supabase/

# ---- measurement sources ----
# art/src holds the untouched Riot ward icons the recoloured ones were made
# from. The site renders the recoloured copies; these are kept so the tint can
# be redone, and are not part of the site.
art/src/

# ---- local tooling ----
serve.bat
TESTING.md
data-freshness.html
